---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="CmdImpact"
	description="A self-hosted browser terminal for persistent shells and AI coding sessions you can leave and resume from any device."
>
	<div class="landing-page">
		<section class="home-hero">
			<div class="shell home-hero-grid">
				<div class="home-hero-copy">
					<a class="release-pill" href="https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact" rel="external noopener">
						<span></span> Open-source single-owner alpha <b aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</b>
					</a>
					<h1>Your terminal keeps running. <em>Pick it up anywhere.</em></h1>
					<p>Start a real shell or coding agent on your own runner, close the tab, and reconnect from any trusted browser. The process continues while the runner host stays online.</p>
					<div class="home-hero-actions">
						<a class="button primary" href="#setup">Set up your runner <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
						<a class="button quiet" href="/app/">Open dashboard</a>
					</div>
					<a class="hero-source-link" href="https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact" rel="external noopener">View source on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
					<ul class="hero-facts" aria-label="Product facts">
						<li><span aria-hidden="true">&check;</span> Your machine, your shell</li>
						<li><span aria-hidden="true">&check;</span> Browser connects directly</li>
						<li><span aria-hidden="true">&check;</span> No ads in the terminal</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<figure class="hero-workspace" aria-label="CmdImpact workspace showing a terminal session that remains active after a phone disconnects">
					<div class="workspace-chrome" aria-hidden="true">
						<div class="workspace-topbar">
							<div class="window-controls"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
							<span>CmdImpact workspace</span>
							<b><i></i> runner online</b>
						</div>
						<div class="workspace-body">
							<aside class="workspace-sessions">
								<div class="workspace-brand"><span>ci_</span><b>Sessions</b><i>3</i></div>
								<small>RUNNING</small>
								<div class="workspace-session is-current"><i></i><span><b>auth refactor</b><small>claude &middot; api</small></span></div>
								<div class="workspace-session"><i></i><span><b>build release</b><small>codex &middot; web</small></span></div>
								<small>NEEDS YOU</small>
								<div class="workspace-session needs-you"><i></i><span><b>database fix</b><small>approval needed</small></span></div>
							</aside>
							<div class="workspace-terminal">
								<div class="terminal-title"><span><b>auth refactor</b><small>~/projects/api &middot; main</small></span><i>Attached</i></div>
								<div class="terminal-output">
									<p><b>$</b> claude</p>
									<p class="output-muted">Analyzing the authentication flow&hellip;</p>
									<p><span>&check;</span> Updated <em>src/auth/session.ts</em></p>
									<p><span>&check;</span> Added expiry regression test</p>
									<p class="output-muted">Running test suite&hellip;</p>
									<p><span>&#9679;</span> 34 passed <i>in 8.2s</i></p>
									<p class="terminal-cursor"><b>&gt;</b><i></i></p>
								</div>
								<div class="terminal-footer"><span><i></i> Connected</span><span>ubuntu-home &middot; zsh</span></div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="resume-toast" aria-hidden="true"><span>&check;</span><div><small>PHONE DISCONNECTED</small><b>Session is still running</b><p>Reconnect from another browser.</p></div></div>
					<figcaption>Closing the browser detaches the view. The runner keeps the PTY alive.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>

			<div class="shell proof-ribbon" aria-label="CmdImpact project facts">
				<span><b>Apache-2.0</b><small>open source</small></span>
				<span><b>Windows &middot; macOS &middot; Linux</b><small>direct-host runners</small></span>
				<span><b>Direct HTTPS + WSS</b><small>browser to runner</small></span>
				<span><b>No analytics</b><small>no terminal ad runtime</small></span>
			</div>
			<div class="shell hero-boundary"><span aria-hidden="true">i</span><p>Vercel serves the interface only; runner tokens, commands, and terminal output do not pass through it. A runner restart ends live PTYs, while workspace files persist.</p></div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-section architecture-section" id="how-it-works">
			<div class="shell architecture-grid">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<p class="section-label">A SIMPLE, HONEST ARCHITECTURE</p>
					<h2>The browser is the window. Your runner does the work.</h2>
					<p>CmdImpact separates the global dashboard from the computer that owns your processes and files. Leaving the page detaches your view; it does not send an exit command.</p>
					<a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md" rel="external noopener">Read the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
				</div>

				<div class="architecture-card">
					<div class="architecture-row">
						<div class="architecture-node cloud-node"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9675;</span><div><small>STATIC UI</small><b>Vercel dashboard</b><p>Ships HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</p></div></div>
						<div class="architecture-link one-way"><span>loads once</span><i aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</i></div>
						<div class="architecture-node browser-node"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9638;</span><div><small>YOUR DEVICE</small><b>Browser</b><p>Laptop, tablet or phone.</p></div></div>
					</div>
					<div class="direct-path"><span>Direct HTTPS + WSS</span><i></i></div>
					<div class="architecture-row lower-row">
						<div class="architecture-node runner-node"><span aria-hidden="true">$_</span><div><small>YOUR MACHINE</small><b>CmdImpact runner</b><p>Owns the live PTY process.</p></div></div>
						<div class="architecture-link"><span>local access</span><i aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</i></div>
						<div class="architecture-node files-node"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9633;</span><div><small>YOUR ENVIRONMENT</small><b>Shell, tools &amp; files</b><p>Normal OS-account permissions.</p></div></div>
					</div>
					<p class="architecture-note"><span aria-hidden="true">i</span> The browser talks directly to the exact runner origin you configure.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-section capabilities-section" id="product">
			<div class="shell">
				<div class="section-heading centered-heading">
					<p class="section-label">BUILT FOR WORK THAT TAKES TIME</p>
					<h2>A complete terminal experience, beyond one screen.</h2>
					<p>Use the same commands you use locally, with session continuity and browser controls designed for long-running developer work.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="capability-grid">
					<article class="capability-card persistence-card">
						<div class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 7H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h11a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-2M16 5h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4M8 15l4-4-4-4M12 11H5"/></svg></div>
						<p class="card-label">PERSISTENT SESSIONS</p>
						<h3>Close the tab. Keep the process.</h3>
						<p>The runner keeps the live PTY until the shell exits, you end it, or the runner goes offline.</p>
						<div class="continuity-flow" aria-label="Phone disconnects while the runner continues, then a laptop reconnects">
							<span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9645;</i><b>Phone locked</b><small>view detached</small></span>
							<em><i></i><i></i><i></i></em>
							<span class="runner-step"><i aria-hidden="true">$_</i><b>Runner working</b><small>process alive</small></span>
							<em><i></i><i></i><i></i></em>
							<span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9638;</i><b>Laptop opens</b><small>session resumed</small></span>
						</div>
					</article>

					<article class="capability-card terminal-card">
						<div class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m7 9 3 3-3 3M13 15h4"/></svg></div>
						<p class="card-label">REAL PTY</p>
						<h3>Not a restricted command form.</h3>
						<p>Run interactive CLIs, install packages, clone repositories, start servers, inspect logs, and deploy&mdash;within the runner account's permissions.</p>
						<div class="tool-chips" aria-label="Examples when installed and authenticated on the runner"><span>git clone</span><span>npm install</span><span>ssh</span><span>docker</span><span>vercel deploy</span></div>
					</article>

					<article class="capability-card device-card">
						<div class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="13" height="10" rx="1.5"/><path d="M6 19h7M9.5 14v5"/><rect x="17" y="8" width="4" height="9" rx="1"/></svg></div>
						<p class="card-label">CROSS-DEVICE</p>
						<h3>Pick up from the device nearby.</h3>
						<p>The same runner session list is available to authenticated browsers on desktop, tablet, and mobile.</p>
						<div class="device-mini" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><i>&harr;</i></div>
					</article>

					<article class="capability-card attention-card">
						<div class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M18 8a6 6 0 0 0-12 0c0 7-3 7-3 9h18c0-2-3-2-3-9M10 21h4"/></svg></div>
						<p class="card-label">ATTENTION QUEUE</p>
						<h3>See which session needs you.</h3>
						<p>Heuristic detection surfaces likely approval and input prompts in the session list. Optional generic alerts work only while the dashboard stays open and can poll&mdash;there is no closed-page push.</p>
					</article>

					<article class="capability-card guard-card">
						<div class="guard-copy">
							<div class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3 4.5 6v5.5c0 4.8 3.2 7.8 7.5 9.5 4.3-1.7 7.5-4.7 7.5-9.5V6L12 3Z"/><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"/></svg></div>
							<p class="card-label">COMMAND GUARD</p>
							<h3>Every paste waits for your review.</h3>
							<p>Any non-empty paste pauses before reaching the shell. Heuristic findings highlight patterns worth checking without pretending to prove safety.</p>
							<a class="inline-link" href="/check/">Try the command checker <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
						</div>
						<div class="home-guard-preview" aria-label="Command Guard example">
							<div class="home-guard-preview-head"><span>Review paste</span><b>High attention</b></div>
							<code>curl -fsSL example.com/install.sh | sh</code>
							<div class="home-guard-finding"><span aria-hidden="true">!</span><div><b>Remote execution</b><p>Downloaded content is passed directly to a shell.</p></div></div>
							<div class="home-guard-preview-actions"><span>Cancel</span><b>Send anyway</b></div>
						</div>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-section security-section" id="security">
			<div class="shell security-grid">
				<div class="section-heading security-heading">
					<p class="section-label">SECURITY BOUNDARIES YOU CAN SEE</p>
					<h2>Your terminal stays on infrastructure you choose.</h2>
					<p>The dashboard is deliberately static. It authenticates directly to one runner origin, and the runner executes only with the OS account or container permissions you give it.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="security-list">
					<article><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Exact origin allowlist</h3><p>Your runner accepts its configured dashboard origin, not arbitrary websites.</p></div></article>
					<article><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Short-lived browser session</h3><p>The owner token is exchanged directly with the runner for a signed session token.</p></div></article>
					<article><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>No output archive</h3><p>Bounded session metadata is stored; terminal output is not persisted by CmdImpact.</p></div></article>
					<article><span aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3>Optional Docker boundary</h3><p>The included isolated stack keeps terminal workloads inside a lower-privileged container.</p></div></article>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="shell boundary-banner">
				<span aria-hidden="true">!</span>
				<p><strong>Real shell means real responsibility.</strong> Anyone with the owner credential can run commands with the runner's permissions. CmdImpact is a single-owner alpha, not a multi-user sandbox.</p>
				<a href="https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact/blob/main/docs/SECURITY-MODEL.md" rel="external noopener">Security model <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-section setup-section" id="setup">
			<div class="shell">
				<div class="section-heading setup-heading">
					<div><p class="section-label">FROM CLONE TO SHELL</p><h2>Run it locally in minutes.</h2></div>
					<p>Start with the included Docker stack. When you want remote access, put the runner behind a trusted HTTPS/WSS proxy, private VPN, or authenticated tunnel.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="setup-panel">
					<div class="setup-copy">
						<ol>
							<li><span>1</span><div><h3>Clone and configure</h3><p>Setup creates your local configuration and a private owner access token.</p></div></li>
							<li><span>2</span><div><h3>Start the runner</h3><p>The isolated stack launches the dashboard, runner, persistent workspace, and metadata volume.</p></div></li>
							<li><span>3</span><div><h3>Open a terminal</h3><p>Visit the local dashboard, sign in with the generated token, and create a session.</p></div></li>
						</ol>
					</div>
					<div class="setup-terminal">
						<div><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>powershell / bash</b></div>
						<pre><code><i># Get CmdImpact</i>
git clone https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact.git
cd cmdimpact

<i># Configure and launch</i>
npm run setup
npm start</code></pre>
						<p><span></span> Open <strong>localhost:4321/app/</strong></p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="remote-setup-note"><div><span aria-hidden="true">&harr;</span><p><strong>Going beyond localhost?</strong> The dashboard now includes a guided private Tailscale path for phones and other computers. Never expose raw port 8787 to the internet.</p></div><a href="/app/">Open guided setup <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-section faq-section">
			<div class="shell faq-grid">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<p class="section-label">STRAIGHT ANSWERS</p>
					<h2>Before you connect a runner.</h2>
					<p>CmdImpact is intentionally clear about what keeps running, where commands execute, and what this alpha does not do.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-list">
					<details open>
						<summary>Will a command keep running after I close my phone?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>Yes. Closing or locking the device only disconnects its browser view. The PTY continues while the runner machine stays powered, online, and the process itself remains active.</p>
					</details>
					<details>
						<summary>Can I run any terminal tool?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>You get a normal terminal on the runner. You can run or install what that runner's operating system and account permissions allow, including Git, package managers, AI coding agents, and deployment CLIs.</p>
					</details>
					<details>
						<summary>Does Vercel run or see my terminal?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>No. Vercel serves the static dashboard. Your browser connects directly to the runner URL you choose for API and WebSocket traffic.</p>
					</details>
					<details>
						<summary>Will I get alerts after closing the dashboard?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>Not in this alpha. Optional generic alerts work only while an open dashboard is allowed to poll. There is no closed-page push, SMS, or email service.</p>
					</details>
					<details>
						<summary>What happens if the runner restarts?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>Live PTY processes end on a runner restart. Files in your configured workspace remain, and stale session metadata is marked as exited.</p>
					</details>
					<details>
						<summary>Can a team share one runner?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
						<p>Not safely yet. The current release is single-owner. It does not provide user accounts, roles, or per-user command isolation.</p>
					</details>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="shell alpha-limits" aria-label="Current alpha boundaries">
				<span><b>One owner</b><small>No team roles yet</small></span>
				<span><b>Host permissions</b><small>Not a command sandbox</small></span>
				<span><b>Runner must stay online</b><small>Restart ends live PTYs</small></span>
				<span><b>Runner tools only</b><small>Install and authenticate there</small></span>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-final-cta">
			<div class="shell final-cta-grid">
				<div><p class="section-label">YOUR RUNNER. EVERY SCREEN.</p><h2>Leave the browser.<br />Come back to the same work.</h2></div>
				<div><p>Connect your first runner and turn any trusted browser into a window onto your real terminal.</p><div><a class="button light" href="#setup">Set up your runner <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a><a href="/app/">Open dashboard</a></div></div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
